{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here","id":465722,"title":"New Storyteller Here!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-01T23:37:39-07:00","id":465722,"title":"New Storyteller Here!","content":"Hey guys, so I've recently become very interested in Scion and I've read almost all of Hero, the Companion, and most of Demigod and Ragnarok. Tonight I finally proposed playing the game to my friends and they want to give it a try. I'm excited at the prospect, however I've never actually DM'd or acted as a Storyteller before so I don't know what to expect. Are there any pointers that you guys might have for me in this endeavor based on your own experiences? Should I stick to the Adventures written up in the Core book or try to make my own? Is a single-pantheon game easier or better than a mixed-pantheon game? Any additional information you'd like to add? Thanks!<br /> <br /> Edit: It may help to mention that I suggested playing it this summer so I have about 2 months to prepare for this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3653,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","user":"TheGraySoul","date":". 04-02-2015, 02:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T10:36:35-07:00","id":466263,"title":"","content":"The most important lesson that you want to learn about being an ST is this; Listen to the players. If the players like action? Then do not make a mystery based chronicle. If they want to be multiple pantheon, then you will be running a multi-pantheon game. Once you talk to them and get a general idea of what they want, then you can plan out the chronicle and go from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T11:36:49-07:00","id":466318,"title":"","content":"My best advice would be to be prepared for how out-of-control it can get. Even beginning Hero characters can be wildly different, and it only gets moreso as the game progresses. This can lead to trouble challenging the group, when you have a group of people invested heavily in different attributes. A challenge that can harm your group tank could possibly annihilate the rest of the party, and a scenario where your Epic Social character has to shine and convince a business magnate to help them out when another rival social character is trying to do the opposite leaves the group's physical types twiddling their thumbs and with no chance to help. All things being well your group will be happy to step back and let the expert in the current situation step up and manage things but it can get tricky in designing conflicts.<br /> <br /> And my favourite piece of advice, which translated over from advice I recall from a ST for Exalted, is that when your players tell you they want to do something outlandish or unlikely the appropriate answer is always &quot;Yes. Now how do you plan to do it?&quot; and let them work toward those way out goals, no matter how unbalancing they may seem (and man does the game get unbalanced and even more out of control at demigod!).<br /> <br /> As regards multi-pantheon or not, your mileage may vary. I've had great experiences with a single-pantheon game (we ran through Ragnarok) and great experiences with a multi-pantheon group where their differences made it harder for the Titans to single out a 'weakness'. That's up to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In playing, if you wanted to run the core book adventures you might find that the Long Road to Heaven adventures are pretty broken in places and need some fixing, and that some of the signature characters in the Hero book are pretty awfully thought out and put together (Eric Donner, for example, has trouble hitting any damn thing with his handgun) but it's a nice framework and structure to try a new game out on. Some of the officially published SAS adventures are good, and better written if you wanted to take a look at them. Otherwise, if you have a great idea, go to it. If you're not sure if the scale of the threats are right maybe playtesting them in a mock-battle might help you check out how the group will fare.<br /> <br /> Overall though, as long as you and your group are having fun it's all good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T13:39:59-07:00","id":466474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=466263#post466263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most important lesson that you want to learn about being an ST is this; Listen to the players. If the players like action? Then do not make a mystery based chronicle. If they want to be multiple pantheon, then you will be running a multi-pantheon game. Once you talk to them and get a general idea of what they want, then you can plan out the chronicle and go from there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Caveat: Don't run a game YOU don't want to just because the players want it. It's a team effort and you're on the team too. In fact, you're like a player/manager in baseball, you don't just manage it, you are IN it. Moreover, you are the one who will be doing the MOST work on the game as well, so it has be something you want to pour your soul into. So, like Augustus, you are <i>prime inter pares</i>, first among equals. Be flexible, but don't be jello-flexible. <br /> <br /> Another caveat: This also refers to players. It is a team. If you have people who want to play REALLY incompatible characters, or someone wants to play a character that would be the kind of person everyone else in the group would hate, revile and oppose in every way possible, there is going to have to be some negotiation. <br /> <br /> Caveat 3: And this REALLY applies in Scion if you are going to be running the Virtues as written. An Aztec Scion with Conviction 5 can be a very scarey being indeed. (Again, how many hearts do I need to cut out to make sure the sun comes up tomorrow?) Having people in your band with Courage 5, you need to expect them to get into a lot of fights and even be seeking out fights when it is absolutely unwise for them to do so. A sniper character with Valor is going to have some problems from the get-go. You can handwave or partially handwave the Virtues to minimize this, get the players on board with creative work-arounds (like the sniper who fires a warning shot) AND just realizing that the two hot-heads who love their high Courage are going to be doing that stuff and having tons of fun with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T14:23:18-07:00","id":466526,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys! That all sounds like a lot of good advice and I'll go into planning this thing with those in mind!<br /> <br /> I've heard that ranged combat isn't as good as melee combat and can be a detractor, however I'm certain at least one of my players is going to want to play a character who uses ranged combat. Is there a good house rule that any of you have seen implemented that can help with this?<br /> <br /> I've been reading through &quot;Long Road to Heaven&quot; and it seems like a good intro for my players and I, but I can definitely see how it will need some tweaks, especially since I'm intending to have my players make their own characters. I think it's a good starting point so I may model some encounters or plots from it into my own story. Do you guys think it would be better to let my players make their characters before I put any work into the story, so that it better reflects their strengths, or is it something that I should work on in conjunction with each other? Thanks again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T01:35:39-07:00","id":469251,"title":"","content":"Also, as a bit of a silly question, how do I determine a certain type of armor's hardness? I've searched all over the core book but there is no clear explanation of hardness even though it's so relevant to combat. Can anyone help me out and point me in the right direction? Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T01:42:33-07:00","id":469252,"title":"","content":"Hardness is an editing mistake. It appears only twice in the entire game line. It was copied over from another system, Exalted, because large parts of Scion's rules were directly copied-and-pasted from that system. *shrug*<br /> <br /> Ignore Hardness and make yourself happier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T01:45:28-07:00","id":469253,"title":"","content":"Oh. Thanks for the help! That's kind of a weird error to make. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T09:37:55-07:00","id":469397,"title":"","content":"Now, you can understand why we all are waiting for the 2nd Edition to come out. Better rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T12:36:49-07:00","id":469527,"title":"","content":"It.. actually happened quite a lot. Scion's rules are very, very poorly written. If you run the game past Legend 3, you'll find that everything starts to fall apart. Mechanics stop working, every roll automatically succeeds, the powers don't scale properly, combat becomes a slog... it's just a mess. It works fine at Hero level (mostly), but Demigod and God are pretty much unplayable without the ST stepping in to fix every problem that comes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:15:54-07:00","id":474533,"title":"","content":"The adventures in the corebook trilogy are not great. I say this having written one of them. :-(<br /> <br /> And Telgar's right: The system starts showing strain even at Legend 4. (It did with my campaign.)<br /> <br /> Other advice: Prep characters and critters in advance. Just writing up NPCs and creatures is good practice for working with the system, and when the players take the adventure into unexpected territory (it *will* happen -- frequently), you'll have something ready to pull out and use. When you create adventures, don't get too attached to the thought of them reaching particular conclusions. Supply a goal to give the players a direction for their characters, but don't insist on it: If the PCs want to do something else, roll with it. Nobody likes being railroaded. Some of my best adventures came just from setting up a situation and letting the PCs react to it.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","user":"DShomshak","date":". 04-09-2015, 10:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T11:30:03-07:00","id":474547,"title":"","content":"Oh -- And don't be put off by warnings about the system. Game systems have problems, you learn to cope with them. (Usually. If you find one system too clumsy or broken for your tastes, well, there's plenty of others.) <br /> <br /> I loved running Scion. It was the best campaign I ever ran. <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:30:02-07:00","id":475049,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advice Dean! I was kind of hoping for some existing structure to work with in terms of a story since I'm rather new to this. I'll probably loosely base my first adventure off of the Long Road to Heaven but I'm going to have to change a lot based on what kind of characters my players play and the type of story they enjoy. I don't know too much about designing NPC's or Monsters but I can probably figure it out based on the templates in the corebook. I'm also in the middle of creating a sample character to use in an encounter with some of the creatures I was thinking about using for the adventure. I'll probably run a few quick battles to see where adjustments need to be made. It's going to be a lot of work but overall I'm looking forward to it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:45:18-07:00","id":475059,"title":"","content":"&quot;but I can probably figure it out based on the templates in the corebook&quot;<br /> <br /> Full stop. No. You don't want to do that, both the premade characters and all the monsters are horribly designed and will either absolutely wreck your PCs with a TPK or they will be so ineffective as to be comedic. (Giants in particular can't hit the broadside of a barn).Something about their designer not having communication with the mechanics people and they were built using an entirely different system, they assume Strength is the &quot;To hit&quot; stat for one.<br /> <br /> I would recommend just rolling up a few dice pools you think they should use and give them a number to roll + epic successes as you see fit. A good rule of thumb is not to give them more epics than your own PCs have (This is relaxed until Legend 4, Hero scale Epics are fine, other wise its horribly broken) and about twice their DV values if you want them to reliably hit the PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T17:00:21-07:00","id":475079,"title":"","content":"Oh, yikes! Lol it sounds like I'm basically gonna have to design my own system at this point. So start with arbitrary stat blocks for monsters until I play test them and then adjust accordingly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:01:39-07:00","id":475366,"title":"","content":"Pretty much.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To explain.. the example PC's and all the monsters are designed <i>aesthetically</i>. The big, tough, strong guys have tons of Strength and no Dexterity. Makes sense, right? Except... that in the combat system Scion uses, that means they will <i>never hit anything</i>. Sure, if they somehow did, it would be devastating... but they won't. Ever. It's not actually possible. They can try to run around that with the Clinch maneuver, but it has pretty serious drawbacks, and it means a Strength-based character (PC, giant, monster, etc) will always and forever have only <i>one</i> option in combat. Which makes that terribly boring for a player, and terribly predictable in NPCs.<br /> <br /> The example characters and the monsters are given all the dots they need to meet their <i>concept</i>... but none of the ones they need to succeed mechanically. There are very definite ways to build a character <i>wrong</i> in Scion, which is unfortunate. It should be totally viable to be a Strength-heavy, Dexterity-minimal character! That's a valid mythological archetype! It shows up all over, in all kinds of media. But it <i>does not work</i> in this system, because they will never hit anything, ever. It's similarly impossible to build a poison-using character, or a beast-master character, or any number of other very common character types. The system just doesn't support them. After Legend 3, it doesn't support firearms. You have to go with bows or thrown weapons, because Firearms don't get any Strength added to their damage. After Legend 3, that becomes a <i>serious</i> problem. Scion also doesn't support turtle builds, where you laugh off any damage. There are too many ways to break through it. Defense-centric is not a good way to go. <br /> <br /> If you already <i>know</i> Scion in and out, you can build a very powerful character... provided you go only for the Boons, Knacks, Attributes and Abilities that actually <i>work.</i> If you don't know which ones are good and which ones are bad, it's very easy to build yourself a really impressive character with tons of powers... that will never accomplish anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","user":"Telgar","date":". 04-10-2015, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T22:31:54-07:00","id":475425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=475366#post475366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty much.<br /> Scion also doesn't support turtle builds, where you laugh off any damage. There are too many ways to break through it. Defense-centric is not a good way to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have found the opposite, its actually extremely difficult for two relatively equal characters to even do damage to one another at all. I have started with a legend 3, defense 14 character with 15L/20B soak and damage conversion to knock it all to bashing, along with bulletproof armor. Granted he was totally maximised for combat, but its possible to have such high defensive stats that any equivalent legend character might as well not bother attacking you. Rock paper scissors is a less time consuming way to fight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3835-\u00falfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","name":"\u00dalfh\u00e9\u00f0nar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T23:13:32-07:00","id":475445,"title":"","content":"That depends on if you've fixed Untouchable Opponent. If not, then yes, it's essentially impossible for anyone to hit anyone else. There are some powers, like Animal Aspect, that can only apply to attack, not defense, so generally in Legend 4+ Scion games, offense wins.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T23:17:13-07:00","id":475446,"title":"","content":"Hmm, that all sounds rather frustrating. Would upping the dexterity and lowering the strength of those monsters a little, help balance them some? It sounds like there's really only one way to go in terms of combat characters which isn't always fun. Honestly, the more I'm hearing about the problems with the system, the more I'm starting to think I've gotten in over my head lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:54:49-07:00","id":475902,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of existing house rules that you can use that will fix a lot of the aforementioned problems. Just be sure to introduce them to your players as early as possible. I've been playing Scion for three or four years using house rules and it's been perfectly fine for my group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:22:28-07:00","id":475930,"title":"","content":"And keep it combat focused. <br /> <br /> Social characters are either omni-powerful or nothing at all. And all the stats bleed together. There's really no difference between a Manipulation and Charisma character except which Knacks they get. Anything one can do, the other can as well. The difference is how they stunt/describe it. So social characters will step all over each other. And social characters can pretty much do ANYTHING social: Want to walk into the White House and make the President your best friend? Check. Want to talk the other players into being your willing slaves? Check. Want to go on TV and convince everyone that blue should be the same as green from now on? Check. Etc. All that is within reach at HERO and effortless at starting Demigod. And trust me, is sounds much much much better than it is. Also, no real rules for what happens when you have a &quot;dance off&quot; between two social characters. Add to that, that a physical primary character can effectively &quot;minor&quot; in social stats and be as powerful in the social arena as a character who specializes in it (since they only need to invest in one stat to cover all the same ground). <br /> <br /> Storytellers and players can smooth some of that out with a lot of cooperation and hand-waving, plus some attempts to nudge things via some House Rules. But chances are good it will get irksome at some point. <br /> <br /> Mental characters are pretty much nothing at all. It's not worth the time to try it. &quot;Smart&quot; gods are one of the archetypes that the game just doesn't support, or it doesn't really do anything to make them worth playing as there are no real rules about what Epic Intelligence, etc can actually DO and the Knacks are less than stellar. Oh, except for some combat adds here and there. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:41:35-07:00","id":475941,"title":"","content":"I haven't run into this in any of the games I've run. I use resistance rolls to resist mental traits and I have specific rules regarding the separate social and mental traits, and what they do. For example, there's a character who has ridiculous Wits and Integrity, so it's incredibly difficult to enter his mind and use the social machinations. There's also a Manipulation heavy character who is crap at being social, but can just manipulate really well, so the band just uses them if they need someone to be quickly interrogated using not-so-ethical means. As well, if you have an Artistry or Forge Purview, you can do some really cool things with Epic Intelligence and Academics/Art.<br /> <br /> I've also found a lot of players will understand the limitations of their own character's personality, so a character who is really Charismatic and honest may not even think about doing something manipulative or two different mental characters use it in different ways, even when they both have Epic Intelligence - like one being a physicist and the other an archaeologist.<br /> <br /> You can fix it and it can be really fun and rewarding for players who specialize in that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","user":"StarkJunior","date":". 04-10-2015, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T01:35:44-07:00","id":476772,"title":"","content":"I find it greatly rewarding to offer, uh rewards, to players who play to type or theme.<br /> <br /> One of Thor's kids who wanted to be a 'baby Thor' and follow in dad's footsteps is going to have some trouble hitting. Obviously, if the player didn't want to take Epic Dexterity, something like Animal Aspect is going to help with that but that's just cherry picking a single boon in a purview they otherwise have no interest in and it's kind of discordant. If the player came up with an inventive way to level the playing field with the thematic powers and birthrights at the character's disposal (and there are some great ways to do that) I'd reward them for being inventive.<br /> <br /> That also helps in the matter of social powers, which are terrifying. A starting character, right off the bat, with God's Honest and little else could probably get to anyone they wanted to with a little basic planning and some roleplay. At that point they can convince that someone (the president, Donald Trump, Zayn Malik) of just about anything. But if I know what the 'theme' of the characters are I can at least plan ahead. Not enough. I mean you pretty quickly lose any semblance of control of how the Scions walk in the world. But I can at least have some idea what to expect and I can make requests. Like 'Pleasepleaseplease, I would prefer that nobody makes characters who want to go straight out and mind control the president.'. Sooner or later the public is going to find out, and the social characters are going to earn their money in smoothing things along, but it's easier for me as a ST when they're the good guys and not some kind of divine occupying force. And those players who play to their theme I reward because it's like me saying 'Thank you for playing in a way I can kind of predict and thus design things with you in mind'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T07:51:47-07:00","id":476944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheGraySoul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=475446#post475446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, the more I'm hearing about the problems with the system, the more I'm starting to think I've gotten in over my head lol.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StarkJunior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=475902#post475902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of existing house rules that you can use that will fix a lot of the aforementioned problems. Just be sure to introduce them to your players as early as possible. I've been playing Scion for three or four years using house rules and it's been perfectly fine for my group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sincerely love Scion, but the mechanics begin to fall apart somewhat early. Stark Junior has the best advice I can recommend. Scion has been out for years, and there are some really impressive house rules you can find that smooth out the vast majority of issues with the game. You just have to introduce them to your group sooner rather than later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T10:43:22-07:00","id":477080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StarkJunior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=475941#post475941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't run into this in any of the games I've run. I use resistance rolls to resist mental traits and I have specific rules regarding the separate social and mental traits, and what they do. For example, there's a character who has ridiculous Wits and Integrity, so it's incredibly difficult to enter his mind and use the social machinations. There's also a Manipulation heavy character who is crap at being social, but can just manipulate really well, so the band just uses them if they need someone to be quickly interrogated using not-so-ethical means. As well, if you have an Artistry or Forge Purview, you can do some really cool things with Epic Intelligence and Academics/Art.<br /> <br /> I've also found a lot of players will understand the limitations of their own character's personality, so a character who is really Charismatic and honest may not even think about doing something manipulative or two different mental characters use it in different ways, even when they both have Epic Intelligence - like one being a physicist and the other an archaeologist.<br /> <br /> You can fix it and it can be really fun and rewarding for players who specialize in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all of that isn't in RAW. You have to write up your own system. And discard what's in place. <br /> <br /> You have to add in Industry/Forge/Art to make Intelligence even remotely useful, but even then, the non-combat Knacks for Mental stats are incredibly lame, completely broken or inappropriate. There are a few exceptions, but not enough to make it interesting. Either you take crap knacks, interesting but nearly powerless knacks, or the few good knacks that everyone else with Epic Mentals has. <br /> <br /> So, to make those characters playable and interesting, you need to:<br /> -Completely overhaul the social rules<br /> -Create at least one, but probably more complete Purviews<br /> -Create a whole slew of new Knacks. <br /> <br /> Hence, if you are starting a new game with RAW and don't want to reconstruct the game or try to knit something together from a patchwork of House Rules from a variety of different sources that are almost all built to the specifications of the home game in which they are played, you should keep it combat focused.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T12:43:02-07:00","id":477180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=477080#post477080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to add in Industry/Forge/Art to make Intelligence even remotely useful, but even then, the non-combat Knacks for Mental stats are incredibly lame, completely broken or inappropriate. There are a few exceptions, but not enough to make it interesting. Either you take crap knacks, interesting but nearly powerless knacks, or the few good knacks that everyone else with Epic Mentals has. <br /> <br /> So, to make those characters playable and interesting, you need to:<br /> -Completely overhaul the social rules<br /> -Create at least one, but probably more complete Purviews<br /> -Create a whole slew of new Knacks. <br /> <br /> Hence, if you are starting a new game with RAW and don't want to reconstruct the game or try to knit something together from a patchwork of House Rules from a variety of different sources that are almost all built to the specifications of the home game in which they are played, you should keep it combat focused.</div> </div> </div> </div>Respectfully, I think you are sending the wrong message here. You are painting everything in shades of doom and possibly discouraging a new player from giving the system a try. You are absolutely right that you need a nice set of house rules to get the most mileage out of the game, but there are a few great ones that are really easy to find! Here is a link to the <a href=\"http://www.herosjourneyrpg.com/forum/showthread.php?tid=21\" target=\"_blank\">JSR Compendium</a>, and here is a link to the <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion 2.0 Fan Project</a>.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, does the system need a big overhaul? Yeah. Can you easily find house rules that make it playable? Also yeah. So give it a try, TheGraySoul! We're all here to support and help you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T14:00:37-07:00","id":477270,"title":"","content":"...Eh. Sure, you could use a system patch like those you provided, but that's basically a whole revamp of the game. You have to print those out, or keep them handy electronically, and they're <i>not</i> small tweaks. It isn't like fixing Untouchable Opponent by cutting the bonus down to 1:1 instead of Epic Scalar. Applying a wholesale system revamp isn't really something a new ST should be diving into. Scion, itself, is not something a new ST should be diving into <i>because it requires all that work to function</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm really sorry to say it, because Scion is full of fun and nifty ideas, but the system is <i>broken</i>. It does not <i>work</i>. So my advice to TheGraySoul is to hold off on running Scion. Wait until the next edition comes out in a year or so. In the mean time, try a different system. Gods and Heroes is a very lightweight system that handles similar themes to Scion. You could probably use a Savage Worlds system to mimic Scion, too. Any number of Superhero systems would work. Even Exalted might be a viable system. Scion... just isn't. Not out of the book. Not without a massive effort to correct it. Not without a lot of experience running games and fixing rules on the fly.<br /> <br /> Because unless you make characters <i>for</i> them, your PC's are going to run into a lot of problems and it is almost certain that someone is going to go after a build that just <i>doesn't work</i>. They'll have wasted all their time and be utterly useless to the party. That isn't fun for anybody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T15:29:39-07:00","id":477352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=477270#post477270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Eh. Sure, you could use a system patch like those you provided, but that's basically a whole revamp of the game. You have to print those out, or keep them handy electronically, and they're <i>not</i> small tweaks. It isn't like fixing Untouchable Opponent by cutting the bonus down to 1:1 instead of Epic Scalar. Applying a wholesale system revamp isn't really something a new ST should be diving into. Scion, itself, is not something a new ST should be diving into <i>because it requires all that work to function</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm really sorry to say it, because Scion is full of fun and nifty ideas, but the system is <i>broken</i>. It does not <i>work</i>. So my advice to TheGraySoul is to hold off on running Scion. Wait until the next edition comes out in a year or so. In the mean time, try a different system. Gods and Heroes is a very lightweight system that handles similar themes to Scion. You could probably use a Savage Worlds system to mimic Scion, too. Any number of Superhero systems would work. Even Exalted might be a viable system. Scion... just isn't. Not out of the book. Not without a massive effort to correct it. Not without a lot of experience running games and fixing rules on the fly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just can't get behind telling an interested player that they should go play another game. That's not the kind of positive and encouraging environment we really want to build here, is it? It doesn't require a lot of work to use those houserules if you are willing to start using them right from the beginning, or at least introduce your players to those house rules first. Speaking from experience, It's totally possible to make the transition pretty smoothly!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T19:37:46-07:00","id":477451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=477352#post477352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just can't get behind telling an interested player that they should go play another game. That's not the kind of positive and encouraging environment we really want to build here, is it? It doesn't require a lot of work to use those houserules if you are willing to start using them right from the beginning, or at least introduce your players to those house rules first. Speaking from experience, It's totally possible to make the transition pretty smoothly!</div> </div> </div> </div>100% agree!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T08:37:42-07:00","id":477950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=477352#post477352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just can't get behind telling an interested player that they should go play another game. That's not the kind of positive and encouraging environment we really want to build here, is it? It doesn't require a lot of work to use those house rules if you are willing to start using them right from the beginning, or at least introduce your players to those house rules first. Speaking from experience, It's totally possible to make the transition pretty smoothly!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is supposedly not just directed to someone new to Scion as either a ST or player, but to someone that hasn't been a ST before, right? I thought that was what the OP was saying. <br /> <br /> I am pretty confident from Charles's previous posts that he has scads of RPG game experience and StarkJr,, I haven't seen as much from you, but you are speaking with a voice that seems freighted with that same weight. I am pretty confidant that you two can both swing running a game that has huge functionality problems, either by handwaving away where RAW doesn't work, by adapting the House Rules of others and/or making up your own. I wouldn't reccomend a new ST put him/herself in that position. Handwaving away the rules is a difficult thing to do. And, for all the amazing work they did, JSR and Scion 2.0 (HR) are, essentially untested House Rules. Both groups have run great games and some of their stuff is damn good, but it's either a complete re-write that has uncovered and created new problems of it's own (take a look at the JSR Fatebinding rules for an example of something that is more detailed but VERY unwieldy). And, Iry, et al. have gotten a significant way into their rewrite, but it is by no means done. Hence, stitching together multiple rules systems. And, until there's a complete set of rules and some play-testing around with groups other than those writing the rules, it is, essentially a meticulously done set of House Rules/Labor of Love. (The kind of play-testing that Scion never got.) Using other people's idiosyncratic rules and adapting them to his/her own game is another thing that a new ST might have issues with. I have seen VERY experienced ST who love tinkering with rules just get up and walk away in disgust at certain points in Scion and done so myself. And that's after six very successful Scion chronicles I have run and one I have played in. <br /> <br /> I LOVE the basic concepts of Scion. They are 100% in my wheelhouse. I scoured used book stores for weird myth books before Scion was a gleam in White Wolf's eye. My MA thesis and PhD dissertation proposal has massive comparative mythology components. Ask Telgar about how insanely into this game and the source material I am. (For that matter, ask Anne about it, where I was the &quot;Hittite&quot; guy - I actually have pictures of the cuneiform tablets with all the Hittite myths on them from Istanbul as part of my screen saver on my TV .)<br /> <br /> For a new guy who wants to run Scion, which I FULLY support him doing, I would recommend the following to mitigate all of the above:<br /> &gt; Use the pantheon write-ups from Scion 2.0 HR (Iry, et al.) when and where you can. If you can get access to the JSR ones use those to plug the holes after Iry. I may have my minor quibbles with their choices here and there, but they are GOOD, SOLID and BETTER than the ones from RAW<br /> &gt; Use Scion 2.0 HR (Iry, et. al.) to expand the Purviews when and where you can. Same caveat about JSR there.<br /> &gt; Make sure every character has a combat function, even if they also have a non-combat emphasis. More &quot;Athena&quot; than &quot;Hephaestus&quot;. Pure combat characters could easily dominate the party and/or the party could all be combatants. That plays to the strengths of RAW. And it obviates most of the need for the rest of the concerns. Plus it's a damn fun game all told. You might need to make sure you've got some decent &quot;gun-fu&quot; rules if anyone wants to play a gun-bunny or sniper type.<br /> &gt; Use the basic essential rule's fixes, like: eliminating Hardness, fixing Untouchable Opponent, maybe something to make ranged combat characters worthwhile (Perception adds is the fast and dirty way to do this), add in some kind of mental resistance. Those are the primary ones I can think of off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> I think you could have a rocking good time with just those fixes up to the Demigod divide. And maybe there might be more official stuff out there to help out by then. <br /> <br /> Or wait until the new Scion system is out and try that one out. Just run something else in the interim. We're doing that right now in my group waiting for Mage20. It sucks, but it is giving me loads of time to work on the next game and we are having fun playing something that we normally wouldn't (Vampire).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd just TRY Scion, either RAW (that's mostly he way I ran the first one + of my Scion games) or with some of the fixes in place up front. But I can be relatively impatient. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-12T14:14:02-07:00","id":478296,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the continued help guys! Yeah Ajax, I am new to STing in general but I have a little experience with playing tabletop games. I played in a short, I'm not even sure if I should call it a campaign but I guess story fits better, of D&amp;D with some friends, and we've also played through the Exalted 2nd Edition adventure Return to the Tomb of Five Corners. Our group for that actually really wants to play EX3 when it comes out but since that's not looking like it will be anytime soon, I offered up Scion as an interim game because I'd read a lot of the books and was interested in it. I'l go through the house rules and see what I can make of them. If I have any more questions I guess I'll post them here, but I'd really like to make at least a couple of introductory sessions work, just to see what my friends think lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T11:12:32-07:00","id":480502,"title":"","content":"Leaving aside questions of house ruling to fix Scion's gaps (I got by with less than 10 pages, including new Knacks and Boons), here's my advice on scenario creation. Other people have asked how to create scenarios; I'll repost what I told them. I think it works for any game, not just Scion. <br /> <br /> (One part is out of date. I refer to my Scioon High campaign chronicle, which I posted some years ago. I'd post a link, but it seems to have vanished along with the old forum, and my Google searches haven't found it yet. Sorry.) <br /> <br /> So: <br /> <br /> I usually have a situation in mind that I think will interest the PCs: some problem they must confront, or some conundrum they must solve. I try <i>not</i> to have particular solutions in mind (unless the challenge is very straightforward, such as, &quot;The monster bursts out and attacks you.&quot;) Half the fun is just seeing how the characters react. Then imagine how NPCs react to what the characters did, which creates a new set of circumstances for the PCs. This requires knowing your NPCs pretty well. <br /> <br /> It is inevitable that PCs will choose options you didn't expect. Sometimes that includes leaving the setting you planned for the scenario. All I can suggest is to try providing enough clues that the players realize that a particular location is where the action is, and these particular characters are the ones with whom they should interact (this guy has the information, that guy is the enemy, the other guy has a common interest, etc.) But now and then, no matter how well you think you planned the scenario or how deftly you planted clues, sometimes the PCs ignore every clue and decide that some tiny peripheral detail is The Center Of It All and go running off to South America, or whatever. You know, like you did with your PCs when you were a player. <br /> <br /> Oh, and here's a trick one of my friends devised when he was GM and it worked so well that everyone in my group uses it when we run games. Start the game with a little vignette for each PC. Maybe some little problem for them to solve. Not necessarily a fight -- it could be pure character interaction, but just some circumstance where they might need to make a decision. It might have some connection to the main scenario, but it doesn't need to. How the characters react may suggest further scenarios, though. When you run these vignettes, be sure to cut quickly from character to character, so players don't sit around for long while they wait their turn. (If you saw my Scion High campaign chronicle thread, you saw how every episode began with these vignettes.) They are a great way to give every character, and player, some time in the spotlight and can help a lot in developing a PC's personality and relationships. <br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T08:31:08-07:00","id":481324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/465722-new-storyteller-here?p=477950#post477950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or wait until the new Scion system is out and try that one out. Just run something else in the interim. We're doing that right now in my group waiting for Mage20. It sucks, but it is giving me loads of time to work on the next game and we are having fun playing something that we normally wouldn't (Vampire).<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd just TRY Scion, either RAW (that's mostly he way I ran the first one + of my Scion games) or with some of the fixes in place up front. But I can be relatively impatient.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a bit of the Mage powerset that's really informing the development of Scion2e, and four members of Team Mage(s) are on Team Scion, so I think the concepts will translate well for your group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T16:05:33-07:00","id":482891,"title":"","content":"What you say interests me, Neall. A while back, my gaming group tried the Dresden Files RPG and found it too annoying to play. I've been thinking that a mashup of Scion and Mage might do the trick, though it would be lot of work to pull together. Hearing that some Mage ideas might make their way into Scion 2.0 suggests there might be less work than I feared.<br /> <br /> One more reason to look forward to Scion 2.0.<br /> <br /> Dean Shomshak","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1175-dshomshak","name":"DShomshak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"197"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}